Add a presentation window for the audience

Purpose: dual-screen lecturing. The lecturer zooms in to write, while
the audience window on the projector keeps showing the whole page.
Toggle on F8 or the canvas menu; Shift+F8 flips it to another screen.

Behaviour:
- Opens fullscreen on the first monitor that is not the lecturer's,
  as a plain window otherwise, so it works without a projector. Not
  persisted: a projector should not reappear on the next launch.
- Everything beside the page is letterbox; the background pattern is
  dropped (ruling is a writing aid for the lecturer only).
- The laser pointer is shown on the audience view while the laser
  tool is active; other pen overlays (selection handles, indicators)
  never are.
- Flip Screen offers every monitor, the lecturer's included, and is
  insensitive without a second screen; it follows the display list.
- Lecturer controls, in a Presentation submenu of the canvas menu and
  on a pen picker button that swaps the sidebar to a presentation
  page (shown only while the audience window is open):
  Lock Page holds the audience on one page while the lecturer scrolls
  (ink on that page still appears); Freeze View holds a still of what
  the audience last saw; Blank Screen shows only the letterbox.
  All clear when the audience window closes, and are pushed onto the
  canvas it follows after a tab switch.
- A windowed audience view re-takes the page shape when the format
  changes; fullscreen is left letterboxed.

Approach:
- Engine: Presentation (crates/rnote-engine/src/presentation.rs,
  engine/presentation.rs) holds audience state per engine, so each
  tab keeps its own framing. The audience camera is not stored; it is
  built per draw from window size and the lecturer's page, so nothing
  needs syncing and redraw needs no mutable engine borrow (the flags
  arrive from inside other borrows; a second borrow could panic).
- Pages tile from the coordinate origin, not the document origin,
  which drifts with infinite-layout padding; frames anchor there.
- UI: crates/rnote-ui/src/presentationwindow/, a passive widget with
  no controllers drawing the lecturer's store, following zoom-window's
  zoomcanvas pattern. Freeze is a texture in the widget, captured by
  rendering the engine off-screen (snapshotting the widget would
  recurse into the frozen branch).
- Rnote ships the icons it names: a devel build has no Adwaita on the
  icon path, so stock icon names render as nothing.

Constraints: builds on zoom-window, which must keep working alongside
it. No change to the file format; nothing changes while the window is
closed.

